The first Sim file, implementing host contracts H2 and H9. It builds on the vendored LibKa0s-Sim-1.0 API as SHIPPED. Read ../LibKa0s/docs/api/Sim/ at the tag first (LK-18: host contract H1-H10, the stub shape and STRINGS). Where it differs from design-sim.md, the shipped doc wins.

Binding cuts (OWNER_SCOPE C.7 and C.8):
- no seam:IsActive and no seam:IsGuarded (activity is the session's `IsActive`);
- one Live, on the seam;
- a second SetProvider for a key that already has one raises;
- Live re-raises the original error value;
- no __newindex wrap: the host asserts `seam:Unwrapped()` is empty.

END STATE
- New core/SimSetup.lua (~80 lines):
  - `local Sim = LibStub and LibStub("LibKa0s-Sim-1.0", true)`;
  - `NS.SimSeam = Sim:NewSeam(NS.Compat, { name = addonName, pure = { GuildBankTabSize = true, GetItemDetails = true, ItemNameQuality = true }, guarded = { QueryGuildBankTab = guardedQuery } })`.
  - Every other Compat function member is wrapped, the BL-06 PlayerName and PlayerClass included: the 13 at core/Compat.lua plus 2, minus 3 pure, gives 12 wrapped.
  - `guardedQuery(tab)` never calls the client. It marks the tab queried in the host's sim world (NS.SimHost), counts `queries`, and schedules the asynchronous reply `NS.Sim:After(0.2, function() NS.Sim:Fire("GUILDBANKBAGSLOTS_CHANGED") end)`. The world and session parts are a no-op until BL-09 and BL-10 exist; guard on NS.SimHost and NS.Sim.
  - NS.SimHost = {} is the HOST's own table for host fields (OWNER_SCOPE C.4). Nothing host-side is ever written onto the library instance or the seam.
  - Degradation: when Sim is nil, nothing is wrapped. NS.SimSeam is a stub with the shipped seam surface (SetProvider a no-op, Live(fn, ...) calls fn(...), Keys and Unwrapped answer {}). NS.Sim is the inert session stub of design-sim §7 as the LK-18 doc states it:
    - IsActive, IsDelivering and IsPanelShown answer false;
    - Fire and DeliverForCleanup answer 0, and After answers nil;
    - Start answers false and the line;
    - RunVerb prints NS.L["The simulator needs LibKa0s-Sim-1.0."] and answers false, "absent";
    - Stop answers false;
    - OnStop, OnStopGuarded, AddListener and the panel members are no-ops;
    - Status answers {active=false}, Session answers nil, and PanelRows and Steps answer {}.
    NS.Sim is defined here as that stub when Sim is absent. BL-10 replaces it with `Sim:New(d)` when the library is present.
- BankLedger.toc: `core\SimSetup.lua` goes on the line straight after `core\Compat.lua`, with the comment '# LOAD-BEARING: wraps every NS.Compat member at load, before any file could read one (Sim-1.0 host contract H2).' Nothing else moves.
- .luacheckrc: a files[] entry only if needed.

TESTS
- New tests/test_sim_seam.lua, registered in tests/run.lua:
  - seam:Keys() equals the sorted 12 wrapped names;
  - seam:Unwrapped() is EMPTY after the whole addon loads (H2, mandatory per C.8);
  - with no session active, every wrapped member answers the mock's live value;
  - SetProvider on a pure key raises;
  - SetProvider twice on one key raises;
  - Live(fn) restores bypass when fn raises, and re-raises the same value;
  - the TOC position: SimSetup is immediately after Compat;
  - a source scan finds no `local x = NS.Compat.X` or `= NS.Compat$` caching outside core/Compat.lua.
- tests/test_surface_parity.lua: a 'LibKa0s-Sim degraded' case. In the degraded arm, `T.assertSurfaceParity(NS.Sim, "LibKa0s-Sim-1.0")` runs against the instance surface registered with Kit.setSurfaceSource in tests/run.lua, plus a seam-stub parity case. In the degraded arm, RunVerb prints the absent line once.
- Existing suites stay green. The idle wrap costs one field test per call.

DOCS
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md: Module Map and the load-order note.
- docs/module-map.md: a SimSetup row.
- docs/compat-layer.md: every member is wrapped by the simulator's seam, the pure three are listed with the reason (constants and real item facts), and QueryGuildBankTab is guarded.
- docs/performance.md: one sentence that the idle seam costs one boolean test per Compat call (about 3,200 per full reconcile pass), with no combat path. The performance-§12 exemption stands.
- Regenerate docs/test-cases.md (CRLF) and move the README Tests badge.

VERIFY
- `ka0s-bounded lua tests/run.lua`: 0 failed.
- `luacheck .`: 0/0.
- `grep -n -A1 'core\\Compat.lua' BankLedger.toc` shows SimSetup on the next line.

Commit `BL-08: ...`. If the shipped Sim-1.0 lacks something this needs, stop. Per OWNER_SCOPE B, the fix lands additively in LibKa0s, the tag moves, and a BL-RV2 refresh follows. Never patch libs/.

The simulated world of req-bl-sim §2. It is runtime-only and lives on the host table NS.SimHost (OWNER_SCOPE C.4), never in SavedVariables and never on the library instance.

END STATE
- New modules/SimWorld.lua (~280 lines). TOC: after modules\Ledger_Diagnose.lua, conventional, before the other Sim modules.
- `SW.Build(opts)` returns a world:
  - chars: main is the real player, read through `NS.SimSeam:Live(...)` (name, realm and class from Compat.PlayerName and PlayerClass). alt is invented: NS.L["Simbanker"], the real realm, and a classFile different from main's;
  - current = "main";
  - bags[charKey], bank[charKey] and warband: the backpack holds 20 slots; C.BANK_IDS' first tab and C.WARBAND_BANK_IDS' first tab hold 98 each; every other id answers 0 slots;
  - guild: a name, which is the real guild name or NS.L["Simulated Guild"] when unguilded; visible = false; 2 tabs of GuildBankTabSize() slots; a queried-tab set; and money;
  - purse[charKey] = 5,000g, warbandMoney = 20,000g, guild money = 100,000g;
  - pool: distinct {itemID, link} from the player's REAL bags, read with `NS.SimSeam:Live(L.ScanStore, L, C.Store.BAGS, links)`. With fewer than 4, it falls back to SessionWindow.lua:203-209's fixed ids (2589, 194863, 171276, 6948), warmed with NS.Item.LoadItem, and reports the fallback once through the debug sink.
- Providers are registered ONCE at file load with `NS.SimSeam:SetProvider(key, fn)` for all 12 wrapped keys (BL-08). Each answers fully from `NS.SimHost.world` and never falls back to live while a session runs:
  - GetContainerNumSlots and GetContainerSlot route by which C.*_IDS group holds the id, returning the same {itemID, link, count} triple Compat answers. An unknown id answers 0 or nil.
  - GetGuildBankSlot answers nil for a tab not yet queried this visit, which keeps OpenContext's QueryGuildBankTabs load-bearing and matches tests/wow_mock.lua:456-457. GetNumGuildBankTabs and GetCurrentGuildBankTab (1) also answer.
  - IsGuildBankVisible answers strictly true or false.
  - GetStoreMoney(store): WARBAND gives warbandMoney; GUILD gives guild.money only while visible, else nil (the F-001 frame-gated semantics, Compat.lua:42-67); anything else gives nil. GetMoney gives purse[current].
  - GetGuildName answers guild.name.
  - PlayerName and PlayerClass answer the current character.
  - QueryGuildBankTab stays guarded. Its provider, if one is needed at all, receives the guarded fn as its fallback.
- A world mutation API for the drivers (BL-10): `SW.Move(charKey, fromGroup, toGroup, itemID, n)`, `SW.Money(...)`, `SW.Switch(to)`, `SW.MarkQueried(tab)` and `SW.ResetVisit()`. These are pure world edits that fire nothing.
- Files stay under 1500 lines, and every function stays at CCN 15 or below.

TESTS. New tests/test_sim_world.lua. Providers are tested directly, as fn(fallback, ...), against a built world, with no session needed:
- each provider's return shape equals Compat's for the same kind of slot (the triple);
- the queried-tab rule (nil before MarkQueried, data after);
- visibility is strictly boolean;
- guild money is nil while hidden and set while visible;
- warband money;
- the purse follows `current` across Switch;
- the identity switch (PlayerName and PlayerClass answer the alt after Switch);
- the pool takes real bag items, and the fallback runs with an empty mock bag and is reported once;
- the unguilded world invents the guild name;
- providers are registered for exactly seam:Keys() minus the guarded key;
- the build reads the real world only inside Live (a spy on the seam's bypass).

DOCS
- docs/module-map.md: a SimWorld row.
- locales/enUS.lua needs no override.
- The ARCHITECTURE localization-§1 row lists the new L keys.
- Regenerate docs/test-cases.md (CRLF) and move the README Tests badge.

VERIFY
- `ka0s-bounded lua tests/run.lua`: 0 failed.
- `luacheck .`: 0/0.
- `grep -n 'NS.db' modules/SimWorld.lua` is empty.

Commit `BL-09: ...`.

The session itself, on the vendored Sim-1.0 (`Sim:New(d)`), plus the event drivers of req-bl-sim §3. One scenario (`bank`) proves the path end to end. The rest come in BL-11. There is NO slash or panel surface yet (BL-12), so the session is driven through NS.Sim in tests.

END STATE
- New modules/SimDrivers.lua (~230 lines). Each driver mutates the world through SimWorld, then fires the client's event sequence through `NS.Sim:Fire`. The event lists are DATA at the top of the file, so a 12.1.5 correction is a one-line edit. The drivers:
  - OpenBank: BANKFRAME_OPENED;
  - CloseBank: BANKFRAME_CLOSED;
  - Deposit and Withdraw with store BANK: BAG_UPDATE(bagID) per touched bag, PLAYERBANKSLOTS_CHANGED(slot), BAG_UPDATE_DELAYED;
  - store WARBAND with `lag` (nil fires both halves together, a number delays the store half through `NS.Sim:After(lag, …)`, and "never" withholds it). The bag half fires BAG_UPDATE plus BAG_UPDATE_DELAYED. The lagged half fires BAG_UPDATE(warbandID) plus BAG_UPDATE_DELAYED. Pending lag handles are counted in NS.SimHost for the gate;
  - store GUILD: BAG_UPDATE, BAG_UPDATE_DELAYED, GUILDBANKBAGSLOTS_CHANGED;
  - Money(store, dir, copper): PLAYER_MONEY;
  - Spend(copper): purse only, PLAYER_MONEY;
  - Loot(item, n): BAG_UPDATE(0), BAG_UPDATE_DELAYED;
  - OpenGuild: visible = true, then GUILDBANK_FRAME_SHOWN; the guarded tab queries then produce GUILDBANKBAGSLOTS_CHANGED after 0.2 s;
  - CloseGuild: visible = false, GUILDBANK_FRAME_HIDDEN;
  - GuildDataAway: the tab changes while visible stays false, then GUILDBANKBAGSLOTS_CHANGED, which must not arm (issue #12);
  - Switch(to): closes an open frame first by firing CloseBank or CloseGuild, then sets current. It fires no PLAYER_ENTERING_WORLD.
- New modules/Sim.lua (~230 lines) builds `NS.Sim = Sim:New(d)` when the library is present, replacing BL-08's stub. The descriptor:
  - name = addonName, seam = NS.SimSeam, slash = "/bl sim", isStoodDown = NS.IsStoodDown;
  - deliver = `function(event, ...) return NS.Ledger:Dispatch(event, ...) end` (BL-05: one lookup, pseudo-events included);
  - scenarios = { names = {"bank"}, defs = { bank = {...} } }. The defs live in modules/SimScenario.lua (TOC after Sim.lua), and each timeline fn is pure;
  - prepare(session, def, opts, ready): builds NS.SimHost.world with SimWorld.Build, sets `NS.State.simLog = {}`, calls `NS.Browser:OnDatasetChanged()` (or the existing dataset-swap entry), opens the ledger window, then calls ready() once. A stale ready is ignored by the library (C.1);
  - play(step): calls the step's driver and answers its detail;
  - refusal(opts), run inside Live, in order (req §6; the library already checks 'already running', and stood-down is checked first here):
    1. stood down: NS.Slash:DisabledLine();
    2. test mode on: L["Turn test mode off before starting a simulation."];
    3. InCombatLockdown;
    4. a real storage frame open (NS.State.openContext ~= nil or a live Compat.IsGuildBankVisible() == true): L["Close the bank first: a simulation cannot run beside a real bank visit."];
    5. NS.Util.VisibilityRefusal().
    A group, an instance or being unguilded is NOT refused;
  - stopText for bank, combat and standDown;
  - a STARTED override carrying the host guarantee ('nothing here is saved');
  - print = NS.Print; debug = NS.Debug with the `Sim` tag;
  - stepDelay = `function(step) return math.max(SIM_STEP_DELAY, step.settle or 0) end`, with the fixed constant `SIM_STEP_DELAY = 1.5`. There is no schema row (C.11).
- Stop hooks:
  - `NS.Sim:OnStopGuarded(function() NS.Ledger:DropContext() end)` runs while the seam still answers, with NO Reconcile. It cancels L._pendingTimer and the settle window and sends SESSION_CHANGED(false);
  - `NS.Sim:OnStop(function(_, reason) NS.State.simLog = nil; NS.SimHost.world = nil; NS.Browser:OnDatasetChanged(); NS.Browser:UpdateTestStrip() end)`.
- Auto-stops (H6):
  - core/BankLedger.lua NS.StandDown (:255) gets `if NS.Sim then NS.Sim:Stop("standDown") end` as its FIRST line;
  - addon:OnCombatChanged (:306) calls Stop("combat") on PLAYER_REGEN_DISABLED, next to the test-mode end;
  - L:Dispatch (BL-05 seam comment): for BANKFRAME_OPENED, BANKFRAME_CLOSED, GUILDBANK_FRAME_SHOWN and GUILDBANK_FRAME_HIDDEN, when `NS.Sim:IsActive() and not NS.Sim:IsDelivering()`, it calls `NS.Sim:Stop("bank")` BEFORE the real handler, so the real open snapshots the real world;
  - real BAG_UPDATE_DELAYED, PLAYER_MONEY and GUILDBANKBAGSLOTS_CHANGED do NOT stop it;
  - a profile reset does NOT end a simulation (C.13). The case is tested;
  - /reload ends it trivially, because nothing is saved.
- Exclusivity:
  - test-mode start is refused while a sim runs (H5). modules/LedgerTable_TestMode.lua startRefusal (:243-252) gains the guard `simulation` with L["Stop the simulation before turning on test mode."];
  - /bl purge is refused during a simulation (C.13). The guard sits in Database:Purge (core/Database.lua:914), which prints L["Stop the simulation first."] and answers false. The same check runs BEFORE StaticPopup_Show at settings/Schema.lua:851-857 and settings/Panel.lua:155-159, so the confirm never opens.
- Debug: the `Sim` tag is declared wherever tests/test_debug_coverage.lua requires tags. There is one line per fired event, guarded query, start, stop and refusal (with its guard).
- Files stay under 1500 lines and every function at CCN 15 or below.

TESTS
- New tests/test_sim_session.lua:
  - each refusal, its exact line and its order;
  - the 'bank' scenario run step by step with `__fireTimers`/`__now`: 3 BANK rows in simLog (2 deposits, 1 withdrawal), the bonus-ID link kept;
  - each auto-stop: a real BANKFRAME_OPENED not delivered by Fire stops it before the real OpenContext, and the open snapshots the mock's REAL containers; combat; stand-down as the first step;
  - the stop order: DropContext runs while the seam still answers, no Reconcile runs after the seam goes off, the pending debounce is cancelled, and SESSION_CHANGED(false) is sent;
  - a profile reset leaves it running;
  - test mode refused while a sim runs, and a sim refused while test mode is on;
  - purge refused through the verb, the panel button and Database:Purge, with the real ledger untouched;
  - db.global.ledger deep-equal and Count unchanged across the run;
  - the guarded QueryGuildBankTab never reaches the mock's client function during a session.
- New tests/test_sim_drivers.lua: each driver's world delta and its exact event sequence (recorded through a spy deliver).
- Extend:
  - tests/test_disabled.lua: while stood down, Start refuses with the disabled line, and Fire answers 0;
  - tests/test_debug_coverage.lua: the Sim tag;
  - tests/test_ledger.lua: the auto-stop branch in Dispatch.

DOCS
- docs/module-map.md: Sim, SimDrivers and SimScenario rows.
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md: the stand-down steps list Sim stop first.
- The localization-§1 row lists the new L keys.
- Regenerate docs/test-cases.md (CRLF) and move the README Tests badge.

