- Every authored file stays under 1500 lines.

Commit `BL-11: ...`.

The player-facing half, under host contracts H7 and H8. Per C.11 the simulator is slash-only: no launcher entry, no key binding, no schema row. The panel position is SESSION-ONLY, so a simulation writes nothing to SavedVariables. This overrides req-bl-sim §8's settings.simPanel and design-sim H10.

END STATE
- settings/Schema.lua NS.COMMANDS gains one feature-verb row, before 'help': `{ "sim", NS.L["Simulate bank visits through the real capture engine; /bl sim for its verbs"], function(rest) NS.Sim:RunVerb(rest) end }`. The dispatcher refuses it while disabled; it is not in HOST_LIVE_VERBS (settings/Slash.lua).
- The generic grammar is the library's: empty, start <bank|warband|guild|onesided>, step, run, pause, resume, restart, stop, status and panel. There are no host verbs, no help verb (C.7) and no per-driver verbs. Each prints one line, e.g. 'Simulation step 3 of 9: deposit 20 × Linen Cloth to Warband Bank (1 recorded).'
- The descriptor gains `panel`:
  - title = NS.BRAND_NAME .. " - Simulation";
  - stepLabel, building labels like 'Deposit 20 × Linen Cloth to Warband Bank' from the step and the real item name;
  - stepTip: what the step injects plus what was recorded, e.g. 'Moves 20 × Linen Cloth from the backpack to warband tab 1; the warband half lands 1.5 s later';
  - startTip and stopTip;
  - anchorTo = `function() return NS.Browser:GetWindow() end` (beside the ledger window, never over it);
  - check = NS.Icon("confirm"), host-passed and already declared;
  - store = a file-local session-only table, `local panelState = {}`, never NS.db;
  - the library's default button and GameTooltip.
  The frame is named BankLedgerSimPanel by the library from `name`. Start, via prepare, also opens the panel.
- The marker (preview-mode, WS-03 and WS-07; #97 covers an unmarked session):
  - while DatasetKind()=="sim", B:UpdateTestStrip sets `strip.text` to `NS.L["Simulation: %s - nothing here is saved."]` formatted with the scenario label, and shows the strip and the reserve. The red title badge is NOT shown for sim; it is test mode only;
  - modules/SessionWindow.lua gets its own W.TestStrip with the same text while NS.State.simLog is set, because it draws sim rows. It is anchored under its title bar, with its rows shifted by the same HEIGHT+4 reserve;
  - both read the one predicate, Database:DatasetKind;
  - a listener (`NS.Sim:AddListener`) repaints both on start and stop.
- Diagnostics:
  - modules/Diagnostics.lua: X.State (:69-79) gains a `simulation=` line;
  - a new `{ "sim", X.Sim }` section in X.Sections (:286-289) reports active, scenario, step pos/total, the current character, simLog rows, events fired, guarded queries and seam:Keys() count, from NS.Sim:Status() merged with NS.SimHost fields;
  - modules/Ledger_Diagnose.lua prints the header line 'simulation running: Compat answers are simulated' when NS.Sim:IsActive() (R9).
- Files stay under 1500 lines, with SessionWindow.lua at 699 plus a little.

TESTS
- tests/test_slash.lua: the sim row exists; /bl sim prints status plus usage and opens the panel; each verb routes to RunVerb; the row is refused while disabled with exactly one line (this extends tests/test_disabled.lua's feature-verb census at :605).
- New tests/test_sim_panel.lua, using NS.Sim:PanelRows() and never __ fields:
  - rows are Start, one per step and Stop, with commands '/bl sim start <name>', '/bl sim step' and '/bl sim stop';
